cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this work, please cite it as below."
title: "Clinic Overbooking with No-Show Prediction: Calibrated Risk, Cost-Aware Optimisation, and a Fairness Audit"
authors:
  - family-names: Sivakumar
    given-names: Yogarajan
version: 1.0.0
date-released: 2025-12-15
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/Yogarajan12/clinic-overbooking-optimization"
abstract: >-
  A four-stage study pairing interpretable machine learning with operations
  research on the Kaggle Medical Appointment No-Shows dataset. Isotonic-calibrated
  no-show risk feeds a Poisson-Binomial overbooking cost model solved under an
  overflow-probability constraint, validated by Monte Carlo simulation across
  twelve scheduling policies and audited for who bears the resulting overflow.
keywords:
  - no-show prediction
  - probability calibration
  - interpretable machine learning
  - algorithmic fairness
  - operations research
  - Monte Carlo simulation
